{"method": "item/started", "params": {"item": {"type": "userMessage", "id": "<uuid-416>", "clientId": null, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "This is an authorized test of how tools report ordinary errors. Do every step below in order, even if you expect it to fail. Do not work around a failure and do not retry a step in another way.\n\nStep 1. If you have a tool that runs shell commands, run exactly this command once: cat <P>/hoh-missing\nStep 2. If you have an apply_patch tool, apply each of the following 2 patches with it, one call per patch, exactly as given (absolute paths):\nPatch 1 (update of a file that does not exist):\n```\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: <P>/hoh-missing\n@@\n-hoh-seed\n+hoh-cell\n*** End Patch\n```\nPatch 2 (update whose old line does not match):\n```\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: <P>/hoh-patch-modify\n@@\n-no-such-line\n+hoh-cell\n*** End Patch\n```\nStep 3. If you have a tool that edits files, use it once on <P>/hoh-shell-modify to replace the text no-such-text with hoh-cell.\nStep 4. If you have a tool that writes or creates files, use it once to create the file <P>/TOKEN.txt/hoh-cell with the single line hoh-cell.\nStep 5. Read the file <P>/hoh-missing, then read the file <P>/TOKEN.txt.\nStep 6. Reply with a short note of what each step did, and end your final message with this fenced block, with the token you read in place of TOKEN:\n```hoh-decisions\n{\"nonce\": \"spike\", \"message\": {\"token\": \"TOKEN\"}}\n```", "text_elements": []}], "startedAtMs": 1794879147819, "completedAtMs": null}, "threadId": "<uuid-414>", "turnId": "<uuid-415>", "startedAtMs": 1794879147819}, "emittedAtMs": 1794879147819}
